From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan,tu: Drop waits on binary semaphores nothing will
 signal

WeChat's Flutter engine (a fork of Impeller) waits twice on the
semaphore it passed to vkAcquireNextImageKHR: once in a submit right
after the acquire and again in the submit before vkQueuePresentKHR.
The first wait consumes the payload that AcquireImageANDROID imported
temporarily, so the second one waits on the permanent payload, which
nothing ever signals. That breaks
VUID-vkQueueSubmit-pWaitSemaphores-03238; Qualcomm's driver lets it
pass.

On msm the device runs in VK_QUEUE_SUBMIT_MODE_THREADED_ON_DEMAND. The
second wait is not pending, so vk_queue_submit() starts the submit
thread and vk_queue_submit_move_binary_waits_to_temps() blocks in
vk_sync_wait(VK_SYNC_WAIT_PENDING, UINT64_MAX) forever. The raster
thread never returns, Flutter's platform thread waits for it on the
next surface change and the whole app stops responding. Without the
submit thread the kernel would reject the syncobj, which has no fence,
and the device would be lost instead.

For each binary semaphore whose permanent payload never left the
VkSemaphore, count the submitted signals that no wait or SYNC_FD
export has consumed yet. With the new vk_drop_unsignaled_binary_waits
driconf option, a queue wait on such a semaphore with a count of zero
is dropped, with one warning per process. The first wait still makes
the first submit wait for the acquire fence, and on msm the jobs of one
queue run in submission order, so the work of the second submit still
runs after it. If vkQueueSignalReleaseImageANDROID would drop a wait,
it submits to the queue instead of copying the payloads on the CPU, so
the release fence still follows the work queued before it. Like the
temporary payloads, which a failed submit already consumes, the counts
are not rolled back when a submit fails.

Enable the option for WeChat's processes only.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [application-specific workaround]
